"""The vendor's GLOBAL attribute-id table -- generated, do not edit.

Generated by `tools/re/gen_attr_ids.py` from the `changeParas` sections of BOTH sources:
the app's 174 bundled profiles and Haier's own configFiles for every device class on disk.
⚠️ The bundled profiles alone gave 674 names and are overwhelmingly air conditioners, so a
change report from a washing machine or a water heater decoded to ids nothing could name.

1220 names across 22 device classes,
**zero collisions**, and of the 319 names declared by more than one class every one
agrees. That is what makes these ids *global*, unlike the single-parameter `5Dxx` registry,
which is per class -- the same number is `volume` on one appliance class and a setpoint on
another.

⛔ A name carrying two different ids is DROPPED rather than resolved by picking one -- the
same rule the ambiguous widths follow, because a wrong id addresses a different attribute
and nothing reports it. Widening the source found exactly one in 1,222: `vboxId`, which is
`11a6` on six air conditioners and `0d24` on a VOICE ASSISTANT. Within the appliances this
integration decodes the ids are global, and that is now measured rather than assumed.

These address the `6C01` changed-parameter report and its documented siblings `4C01` (read)
and `5C01` (multi-attribute write).

⚠️ **A number here is not permission to write it.** No published model declares an operation
for any of those commands (all 1,451 products enumerated) and no appliance has been observed
accepting one. ⓘ Nor has any been observed SENDING a `6C01`: six diagnostics downloads
carrying a frame ledger show four kinds (`06/6d01`, `04/0f5a`, `03/0006`, `06/7d01`) and no
change report among them. This is the table such a path would need, not evidence it exists.
"""
